  "mechanism": {
    "headline": "NO-GO on every target. The motivating diagnostic was inflated by an absent task settlement barrier in MY analysis script, not by any property of the candidate.",
    "leak_quantified": "Re-running the motivating repository-by-binary diagnostic on SWE277 CPU with and without the barrier: utility 1787 without it (TP 376 / FP 93) against 100 with it (TP 24 / FP 20). RSS collapses 241 -> -2. Disk, which was never the claim, moves only 165 -> 140.",
    "why": "Agents re-run the same command repeatedly WITHIN a task. Repository-by-binary aggregation looks powerful precisely because it captures that repetition, and the causal contract forbids it: every clause in a task is predicted before any observation from that task settles. Across the barrier, most repositories simply have too little prior cross-task history -- SWE277 holds 277 tasks over 213 repositories.",
    "oracle_gap": "The hindsight repository-by-command oracle remains high (CPU SWE277 2100) while its causal realisation reaches 100, about 5%. The information exists but is not causally available at prediction time. That gap, not representation, is the ceiling.",
    "prediction_check": "The frozen amendment predicted this would help CPU and RSS and not Disk. It helped none of them, so the mechanism claim is falsified as stated, not merely unsupported."
  },
